+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and later features of the toolkit will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, that returns the value a JSON Pointer string refers to.
+- It throws an error when the pointer is not syntactically valid per RFC 6901, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`), and setting, adding or removing values.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: Evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (the project has no source yet), new tests run by `npm test`.
+- Public API of the library gains one export; no dependencies added.
